ORDINANCE NO. ________

ENTITLED: "AN ORDINANCE APPROVING AND ESTABLISHING REVISED
WATER AND SEWER RATES, TAP AND SYSTEM DEVELOPMENT
FEES,
ADMINISTRATIVE
FEES,
SERVICE
CHARGES
AND
PENALTIES, AND SEPTIC AND COMMERCIAL WASTE DUMP
RATES,
AS
RECOMMENDED
BY
THE
BOARD
OF
PUBLIC
UTILITIES."

BE IT ORDAINED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE CITY OF
CHEYENNE, WYOMING:

Section 1.  That, pursuant to WYO. STAT. §15-7-407, the Board of Public Utilities
(“BOARD”) shall fix the rates for water and sanitary sewer services furnished to customers, and
any revision thereof is subject to the governing body’s review, modification, and approval.

Section 2.  That the BOARD is authorized by State Statute and City Code to fix rates,
fees and penalties for water and sanitary sewer services furnished to customers to:
A. Pay interest charges and principal payments on all outstanding water and sanitary
sewer loans and bonds as they are due;
B. Pay for the operation and maintenance of the water and sanitary sewer systems,
including salaries, wages and benefits, and the cost of all materials and supplies
necessary for repairs, replacements and upgrades to the systems;
C. Cover all miscellaneous expenses;
D. Cover all usual extensions and enlargements, together with a reasonable allowance
for emergency and unforeseen expenses; and,
E. Provide and maintain a depreciation fund for each of the water and sanitary sewer
departments.

Section 3.  That the Board has determined that an increase in the water and sanitary sewer
rates are justified to ensure adequate revenue is generated in order to pay for costs associated
with those services rendered.

Section 4.  That, pursuant to City Code Section 13.04.140, rates, and charges for the
consumption of city utility services, charges and fees for connections, inspections, penalties,
shutoff penalties and meter installations shall be established by the BOARD, approved by the
Governing Body and filed with the City Clerk and business office of the Board.

Section 5.  That, pursuant to City Ordinance 4447, adopted on June 13, 2022, prior to the
beginning of each fiscal year the BOARD will calculate new rates for water and sewer services
based on the Bureau of Labor Statistics, Consumer Price Index, All Urban Consumers, Water
and Sewer Maintenance and the Wyoming Cost Living Index – Southeast Region and prepare
new rate schedules for Water and Sewer services.

Section 6.  That the Bureau of Labor Statistics, Consumer Price Index, All Urban
Consumers, Water and Sewer Maintenance for the calendar year 2022 was 4.9% and the
5:50 pm, May 02 2023
```

### Page 2 of 20

```text
2
Wyoming Cost of Living Index – Southeast Region for the second quarter of 2022 was 10.5%;
and the Engineering News Record Construction Cost Index (ENR CCI) for calendar year 2022,
was 7.2%.

Section 7.  That the BOARD established by Resolution No. 2023-04, adopted April 24,
2023, revised Water rates to be charged to users of the Cheyenne Water System as shown and set
forth on the resolution attached hereto as Exhibit A.

Section 8.  That the BOARD established by Resolution No. 2023-05, adopted April 24,
2023, revised Sewer rates to be charged to users of the Cheyenne Sewer System as shown and set
forth on the resolution attached hereto as Exhibit B.

Section 9.  That the BOARD established by Resolution No. 2023-06, adopted April 24,
2023, revised Water and Sewer Connections Fees, System Development Fees, Pump Station
Development Fees, and Related Fees set by the Board of Public Utilities as shown and set forth
on the resolution attached hereto as Exhibit C.

Section 10.  That the BOARD established by Resolution No. 2023-07, adopted April 24,
2023, revised Administrative fees, Service charges and Penalties set by the Board of Public
Utilities as shown and set forth on the resolution attached hereto as Exhibit D.

Section 11.  That the BOARD established by Resolution No. 2023-08, adopted April 24,
2023, revised Septic Waste Dump and Commercial Waste Rates to be charged to the user of the
Cheyenne Water and Sewer Systems as shown and set forth on the resolution attached hereto as
Exhibit E.

Section 12.  That the Governing Body has reviewed the rates, charges and fees
established by the BOARD for water and sewer services and hereby approves the water and
sewer rate schedules attached hereto.

Section 13.  That, prior to the beginning of each fiscal year, the BOARD will calculate
new rates for Water and Sewer services based on the Bureau of Labor Statistics, Consumer Price
Index, All Urban Consumers, Water and Sewer Maintenance, Wyoming Cost Living Index –
Southeast Region and The Engineering News Record Construction Cost Index (ENR CCI) and
prepare new rate schedules for Water and Sewer services that shall be presented, in the form of
an ordinance, to the Governing Body.

Section 14.  That this ordinance shall be in full force and effect upon its passage and
publication.
